From: Bottlerocket Team <bottlerocket@amazon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer tracefs at /sys/kernel/tracing and avoid sed

Upstream hard-codes the ftrace directory as /sys/kernel/debug/tracing, which
only exists when debugfs is mounted. Modern kernels mount tracefs directly at
/sys/kernel/tracing, and debugfs access is restricted under kernel lockdown,
so try /sys/kernel/tracing first and fall back to the debugfs path.

kprobe and uprobe also pipe dmesg through sed to indent error output; use awk
instead, since Bottlerocket does not ship sed.
---
--- a/execsnoop
+++ b/execsnoop
@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@
 # 07-Jul-2014	Brendan Gregg	Created this.
 
 ### default variables
-tracing=/sys/kernel/debug/tracing
+tracing=/sys/kernel/tracing
+[[ -e $tracing/trace ]] || tracing=/sys/kernel/debug/tracing
 flock=/var/tmp/.ftrace-lock; wroteflock=0
 opt_duration=0; duration=; opt_name=0; name=; opt_time=0; opt_reexec=0
 opt_argc=0; argc=8; max_argc=16; ftext=
--- a/fs/cachestat
+++ b/fs/cachestat
@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@
 # 28-Dec-2014	Brendan Gregg	Created this.
 
 ### default variables
-tracing=/sys/kernel/debug/tracing
+tracing=/sys/kernel/tracing
+[[ -e $tracing/trace ]] || tracing=/sys/kernel/debug/tracing
 interval=1; opt_timestamp=0; opt_debug=0
 trap 'quit=1' INT QUIT TERM PIPE HUP	# sends execution to end tracing section
 
--- a/iolatency
+++ b/iolatency
@@ -40,7 +40,8 @@
